{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1574041337,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU1MjQwODgyMzM=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3876","origin":"github"},"title":"Do download and addurl in one pass over the file content","message":"When crawling a dataset with large files (\u003e200GB per file) I noticed that the box (AWS EC2 instance) gets busy re-reading downloaded file by git-annex to compute its key. Ideally the key (checksum) gets computed in one pass along with downloading the data.\nAlthough a long shot, I think we might at some point consider some way to make adding new files avoid such two pass (download + `annex add`) over the file. I don't think the issue is crawler specific, so filing it in the datalad \"core\".","files":null}]}